- op: discuss  # 719c
  at: '2026-10-30T18:36:53Z'  # 719c
  by: agent  # 719c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 719c
  clock: 5  # 719c
  nonce: 719c  # 719c
  message: "Done in PR #1961 (892d4912cb). Root cause: rust.py's use_declaration branch read only a single path child, so a scoped_use_list / use_as_clause emitted no imports edge (and a top-level use {...} emitted one whose module slot was the whole brace text); an aliased call looked up a symbol named by the alias. Fix: the use-tree walker expands every bound path, each resolved as a single path is; an aliased call resolves the alias's PATH (_rust_function_in_module). The change exposed profile.py's Rust import-evidence gap (no :: separator, actix-web vs actix_web), fixed in the same PR. CLOSURE EVIDENCE, the filed fixture (INV-nuzas cargo) through production hypergumbo survey on merged dev: crate-a/src/lib.rs:3  now has an imports edge to crate-b/src/lib.rs (had none); line 8  calls rust:crate-b/src/lib.rs helper (was rust:crate_b:0-0:helper stand-in); 0 workspace-prefixed external_symbol nodes. Controls ctl_rs / ctl_rs2: their crate::m alias calls now resolve to src/m/mod.rs (were stand-ins), nothing lost. Corpus A/B: 5 repos, imports +5,385 / -60 (brace-text stand-ins), zellij 17 alias calls corrected, every call edge read."  # 719c
