  message: "CORRECTION to the closure note above: its evidence sentence was truncated by shell quoting (backticks in the argument ran as a command). The evidence, restated exactly. The filed fixture (INV-nuzas cargo, ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/nuzas_10292026/fixtures/cargo) through production hypergumbo survey on merged dev 892d4912cb: crate-a/src/lib.rs line 3 is use crate_b::{Thing, helper as h2}; -- it imports crate-b/src/lib.rs, recorded on the one deduplicated imports edge to that file, whose meta call_lines is [1, 3] (line 1's use crate_b::helper names the same file; before this change line 3 contributed nothing). Line 8, h2(), calls rust:crate-b/src/lib.rs:2-2:helper:function (was the rust:crate_b:0-0:helper stand-in). 0 workspace-prefixed external_symbol nodes in the fixture. Controls ctl_rs / ctl_rs2: their crate::m alias calls resolve to src/m/mod.rs (were stand-ins); nothing lost. Corpus A/B on 5 repos: imports +5,385, -60 (every one a brace-text stand-in); zellij's 17 aliased calls corrected, every one read."  # e8cd
